###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Only energies are fitted and tested; no force error is given. The model of this paper is the energy-only precursor of DeePMD and is encoded under the registry method entity:DeePMD (alias 'Deep Potential').
# - For copper the reference is a classical EAM potential, encoded as a generic mlips:ReferenceCalculation with LAMMPS as code.
# - The BPNN comparison values (Cu 0.20, Zr 0.21 meV/atom) come from the authors' own BPNN implementation with the Cu symmetry functions of ref. 29; no settings are given, so they are not encoded as runs.
# - No cutoff is stated for C7O2H10. Ablations (no rotational fixing: 0.05 eV; no permutational fixing for Cu: 15.6 meV/atom) are not encoded.
# - The water energy RMSE is per molecule (no unit individual). The software implementation is not named.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).

